WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.729
Module four. Orders. From the moment a new order arrives, to the moment it leaves

2
00:00:05.729 --> 00:00:06.581
The warehouse.

3
00:00:08.767 --> 00:00:13.833
Orders are where the vendor earns money. A fast, correct dispatch keeps customers

4
00:00:13.833 --> 00:00:16.084
Happy and keeps the S L A rate high.

5
00:00:16.534 --> 00:00:20.396
First, the new order alert, and what accept and dismiss really do.

6
00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:23.150
Then verifying and accepting the order.

7
00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:26.693
Then the order stages: pick, pack and hand over.

8
00:00:27.143 --> 00:00:31.644
Then the two ways to dispatch: Shiprocket, or the vendor's own local driver.

9
00:00:32.094 --> 00:00:34.270
Then WhatsApp pickup slots and tracking.

10
00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:38.198
And finally, delivery timing, and what is still being worked on.

11
00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:45.629
Every order moves through the same stages. Each stage the vendor updates is mirrored

12
00:00:45.629 --> 00:00:48.024
In the customer app and the admin panel.

13
00:00:48.474 --> 00:00:50.693
A new order alert appears, with a sound.

14
00:00:51.143 --> 00:00:53.959
The vendor checks the items and stock, and accepts.

15
00:00:54.409 --> 00:00:57.566
Verify and pick: the goods are taken from the shelf.

16
00:00:58.016 --> 00:01:00.981
Verify and pack: the goods are packed and ready.

17
00:01:01.431 --> 00:01:06.466
Hand over: the package goes to the Shiprocket courier, or the vendor's local driver.

18
00:01:06.916 --> 00:01:08.729
And delivered to the customer's site.

19
00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:15.987
When an order arrives, this alert pops up on whatever page the vendor is on, with a

20
00:01:15.987 --> 00:01:16.338
Sound.

21
00:01:16.788 --> 00:01:20.159
It's marked action required, with an auto dismiss timer.

22
00:01:20.609 --> 00:01:24.044
It shows the order I D, the quantity, and the total value.

23
00:01:24.494 --> 00:01:27.758
View and Accept Order takes the vendor straight to the order.

24
00:01:28.208 --> 00:01:32.254
And Dismiss only closes the alert. It does not cancel the order.

25
00:01:32.254 --> 00:01:35.162
The order stays in Orders, waiting for action.

26
00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:40.635
Remember this one, because vendors get it wrong.

27
00:01:40.635 --> 00:01:44.151
Dismiss is not cancel. Dismiss only silences the alert.

28
00:01:44.151 --> 00:01:49.456
The order is still sitting in Orders, under awaiting action, and the clock is still

29
00:01:49.456 --> 00:01:54.314
Running. To refuse an order, the vendor must open it and click cancel order.

30
00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.348
Opening the order shows its details.

31
00:02:36.798 --> 00:02:39.123
The order I D and the delivery area.

32
00:02:39.573 --> 00:02:44.352
Product verification. The vendor ticks each item after checking it's really there.

33
00:02:44.802 --> 00:02:47.447
Available stock is shown next to each item.

34
00:02:47.897 --> 00:02:50.948
Cancel order, if the vendor truly cannot fulfil it.

35
00:02:51.398 --> 00:02:56.616
And verify and accept. The status updates for the admin and the customer at the same

36
00:02:56.616 --> 00:02:57.051
Moment.

37
00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:02.368
Back on the orders page, every order is tracked here.

38
00:03:02.818 --> 00:03:05.787
Awaiting action counts orders not yet accepted.

39
00:03:05.787 --> 00:03:07.618
This should be close to zero.

40
00:03:08.068 --> 00:03:10.906
Filters by status, warehouse and payment type.

41
00:03:11.356 --> 00:03:16.092
The status column: accepted, picking, packed, dispatched, delivered or cancelled.

42
00:03:16.542 --> 00:03:19.635
And the action menu, to move the order to the next stage.

43
00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:26.428
When the order is packed, the vendor clicks dispatch, and chooses one of two tabs.

44
00:03:26.878 --> 00:03:32.358
Shiprocket courier, automatic. Shiprocket chooses the best available courier, like

45
00:03:32.358 --> 00:03:37.838
Delhivery, Blue Dart or Shadowfax, assigns an A W B tracking number, generates the

46
00:03:37.838 --> 00:03:41.580
Shipping label, and schedules pickup from the warehouse.

47
00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:44.520
Customer S M S updates come from Shiprocket.

48
00:03:44.970 --> 00:03:50.889
Local or in-house driver. The vendor uses their own driver, picked from Drivers and

49
00:03:50.889 --> 00:03:56.665
Fleet, with name, phone and vehicle. Important: in this case no S M S goes to the

50
00:03:56.665 --> 00:04:00.160
Customer, because S M S is handled by Shiprocket.

51
00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:04.487
Let's watch this in the live demo.

52
00:04:07.500 --> 00:04:12.769
Here's the dispatch window from the live demo. This tab is Local or In-house driver.

53
00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:20.183
The vendor can select a saved delivery partner from the drop down, or type the

54
00:04:20.183 --> 00:04:23.905
Driver's name, phone number, vehicle model and vehicle number.

55
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.728
Then dispatch with the local driver. Remember, the customer won't get an S M S for

56
00:04:36.728 --> 00:04:37.047
This.

57
00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:45.837
Now the Shiprocket courier tab. It shows the automated courier assignment, the

58
00:04:45.837 --> 00:04:48.631
Destination pincode, and the pickup warehouse.

59
00:04:49.231 --> 00:04:54.812
The vendor clicks dispatch via Shiprocket. But here a notice appears: Shiprocket did

60
00:04:54.812 --> 00:04:57.935
Not assign an A W B with any available courier.

61
00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:08.624
The reason was the one we saw in module three. This warehouse's pickup address was

62
00:05:08.624 --> 00:05:10.561
Not yet verified in Shiprocket.

63
00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:24.217
That's why the agreed fix is to verify every pickup address before approving the

64
00:05:24.217 --> 00:05:27.991
Warehouse. The error text will also be made clearer for vendors.

65
00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:38.220
Let's watch this in the live demo.

66
00:05:41.233 --> 00:05:44.860
This is the same order inside the Oribrix Shiprocket account.

67
00:05:47.633 --> 00:05:52.999
Notice the yellow tag: e-way bill mandatory. The order is worth over sixty four

68
00:05:52.999 --> 00:05:56.124
Thousand rupees, so an e-way bill is required.

69
00:05:56.724 --> 00:05:59.678
And under pickup address, a red dot: unverified.

70
00:05:59.678 --> 00:06:02.078
That's the cause of the dispatch error.

71
00:06:02.678 --> 00:06:05.900
From the menu, the order can be marked as verified.

72
00:06:05.900 --> 00:06:09.249
Shiprocket confirms: one order verified successfully.

73
00:06:14.033 --> 00:06:17.980
Once Shiprocket accepts the order, a few things happen automatically.

74
00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:20.286
A delivery partner is assigned.

75
00:06:20.736 --> 00:06:25.610
A WhatsApp message goes to the vendor's registered phone, with a pickup time slot,

76
00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:29.653
For example ten in the morning to two in the afternoon the next day.

77
00:06:30.103 --> 00:06:33.922
The vendor can confirm the slot, or change it, right in WhatsApp.

78
00:06:33.922 --> 00:06:37.740
So the vendor's registered number must be a real, working number.

79
00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.793
The courier picks up the package with the shipping label.

80
00:06:41.243 --> 00:06:43.440
A live tracking link becomes available.

81
00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.362
And the order is delivered.

82
00:06:47.767 --> 00:06:52.646
One honest point from the session. Oribrix is a quick commerce business, and speed

83
00:06:52.646 --> 00:06:53.122
Matters.

84
00:06:53.572 --> 00:06:58.682
Today, with Shiprocket, assigning a delivery partner can take about twelve to twenty

85
00:06:58.682 --> 00:07:01.785
Four hours. That's fine for bulk and long distance.

86
00:07:02.235 --> 00:07:07.756
But the Oribrix goal is instant delivery, in one to two hours, especially for medium

87
00:07:07.756 --> 00:07:12.816
Value city orders, like lights or boards worth ten or twenty thousand rupees.

88
00:07:13.266 --> 00:07:18.498
So faster options are being explored. Porter offers express delivery, but only on

89
00:07:18.498 --> 00:07:22.826
Two wheelers and only in some cities, so it can't carry bulk loads.

90
00:07:22.826 --> 00:07:24.893
Other options are being checked.

91
00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:31.503
Here are the order statuses you'll see in the orders list, and what each one means.

92
00:07:31.953 --> 00:07:36.943
New, or awaiting action. The order has arrived, but the vendor hasn't accepted it

93
00:07:36.943 --> 00:07:38.545
Yet. The clock is running.

94
00:07:38.995 --> 00:07:41.939
Accepted. The vendor checked and confirmed the items.

95
00:07:42.389 --> 00:07:45.951
Picking, then packed. The goods are being prepared in the warehouse.

96
00:07:46.401 --> 00:07:50.497
Dispatched, or in transit. It has been handed over and is on the way.

97
00:07:50.947 --> 00:07:53.959
And delivered or cancelled, the two final states.

98
00:07:53.959 --> 00:07:57.155
A cancelled order should always have a clear reason.

99
00:07:59.567 --> 00:08:03.843
Cancelling hurts the customer and the vendor's rating, so it should be rare.

100
00:08:03.843 --> 00:08:06.543
Here is when it's acceptable, and when it isn't.

101
00:08:06.993 --> 00:08:11.284
When the stock really isn't there. And then fix the stock number straight away, so

102
00:08:11.284 --> 00:08:12.540
It doesn't happen again.

103
00:08:12.990 --> 00:08:15.912
When the item is damaged and there's no replacement.

104
00:08:16.362 --> 00:08:18.133
When the customer asks to cancel.

105
00:08:18.583 --> 00:08:23.404
Never just to avoid a small order. The minimum order quantity exists for that.

106
00:08:23.854 --> 00:08:28.377
And never because dispatch looks hard. Ask the Oribrix team for help instead.

107
00:08:30.767 --> 00:08:32.687
Here's a checklist for every order.

108
00:08:33.137 --> 00:08:35.078
Accept within minutes, not hours.

109
00:08:35.528 --> 00:08:38.280
Tick each item only after physically checking it.

110
00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:42.485
Update pick and pack stages honestly. The customer sees them.

111
00:08:42.935 --> 00:08:47.200
If the order is fifty thousand rupees or more, upload the e-way bill.

112
00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.375
That's module five.

113
00:08:48.825 --> 00:08:52.750
Confirm the WhatsApp pickup slot, so the courier doesn't come back empty.

114
00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:58.672
And if you use a local driver, inform the customer yourself, because no S M S goes

115
00:08:58.672 --> 00:08:58.939
Out.

116
00:09:01.333 --> 00:09:04.559
Quick check. A vendor clicked dismiss on a new order alert.

117
00:09:04.559 --> 00:09:06.965
What happened to the order? Pause and think.

118
00:09:10.915 --> 00:09:15.082
The answer: it's still waiting in Orders, under awaiting action.

119
00:09:15.082 --> 00:09:17.166
Dismiss only silences the alert.

120
00:09:19.967 --> 00:09:23.935
And if a Shiprocket dispatch fails anyway, here's what the vendor should do.

121
00:09:24.385 --> 00:09:25.857
Read the notice carefully.

122
00:09:26.307 --> 00:09:30.275
Don't cancel the order. The goods are packed and the customer is waiting.

123
00:09:30.725 --> 00:09:32.624
Tell the Oribrix team straight away.

124
00:09:33.074 --> 00:09:36.466
The admin checks the pickup address in Shiprocket and fixes it.

125
00:09:36.916 --> 00:09:41.993
Then retry the Shiprocket dispatch, or, if it's urgent, use a local driver and

126
00:09:41.993 --> 00:09:43.294
Inform the customer.

127
00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.471
Let's summarise module four.

128
00:09:47.921 --> 00:09:52.017
The alert has view and accept, or dismiss, and dismiss is not cancel.

129
00:09:52.467 --> 00:09:54.493
Verify each item, then accept.

130
00:09:54.943 --> 00:09:57.439
The stages are pick, pack and hand over.

131
00:09:57.889 --> 00:10:04.012
Shiprocket gives an A W B and customer S M S. A local driver means no S M S.

132
00:10:04.462 --> 00:10:08.384
And an unverified pickup address causes the dispatch error.

133
00:10:08.384 --> 00:10:11.907
Next, in module five, e-way bills, returns and money.

134
00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:19.975
That's the end of module 4. Next up, module 5: E-way bills, returns and earnings.
